{"stack":["1dbb8c66"],"skill":{"name":"merge_to_main","prompt":"Merge the current working branch into main and clean up. Steps:\n1. Check `git status`; commit ALL uncommitted work on the current branch with a clear message, including `.coding/` (plans, knowledge, reviews, backlog.jsonl must land in the merge). NEVER stash — a stash here is never popped.\n2. `git checkout main` → `git merge --no-ff <branch>` (main receives only these merge commits, never a direct one). Conflicts: resolve with file_edit, then `git add` + `git commit`. `.coding/backlog.jsonl` carries git's union merge driver (concurrent adds concatenate); the rest of `.coding/` is plain text.\n3. VERIFY THE MERGED TREE BUILDS before cleanup — branch verification never compiles the src-tauri bin crate. Run BOTH `npm run build` (frontend tsc + vite) AND `cd src-tauri && cargo build` (bin crate). On failure: fix with file_edit, re-run both until green.\n4. Merge commit in main AND both builds green → delete the merged branch (`git branch -d <branch>`).\n5. Supersede stale branch-status memories (memory tools work inside a skill even though absent from the allow-list): memory_recall the branch name and its pre-merge tip commit, memory_list with prefix \"SHIPPED\" (finish digests carry an unmerged-branch hint), and working-tier \"ACTIVE:\"/\"STEP MARKER:\" crash markers citing the branch or its plan. Supersede each stale match with a short successor recording \"MERGED into main at <merge commit sha> (`git rev-parse main`) on <date>\" — never records about other branches or genuinely unmerged work; skip cleanly when nothing matches. The memory index re-derives from the files automatically — never hand-edit or re-derive the DB.\n6. skill_end → Planning. Unresolvable conflicts → abandon_skill (roll back to the pre-skill state). Optional: `git push` via the git tool (approval-gated).","target_state":"planning","pre_skill_state":"complete","tools":["file_read","file_edit","file_write","file_append","shell","sear